 "validity_by_source": {
  "date": "2026-11-01",
  "what": "Accuracy the reader states for writing that is not from the PersonalityCafe typology forum, which is all writing a real user brings.",
  "tested_off_forum_with_mbti_labels": false,
  "why_untested": "No openly downloadable MBTI-labelled writing from outside PersonalityCafe was found (2026-11-01): PANDORA and MBTI9k (Reddit flair) need access requests, Twitter MBTI sets (Plank & Hovy 2015) are tweet IDs only, and the open Hugging Face 'MBTI' sets are PersonalityCafe copies, LLM-made, or of unknown provenance. Nothing was downloaded.",
  "discount_rule": "Letter accuracy off the forum is INFERRED, not measured: the model's AUC against the linked Big Five trait on 2,467 student essays, turned into r and divided by the published MBTI-Big Five link (McCrae & Costa 1989: .74 E, .72 O, .44 A, .49 C). That keeps about 30 to 55% of the in-domain letter r. The same off-forum number is used for every kind of writing; shorter texts scale its lift by the in-domain length curve.",
